'''Holy Coppermine''' is an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]] that can be obtained by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during [[Xmas Gals (Gacha Event)|Xmas Gals]] gacha event. She was added in [[Version 4.5 Update|Version 4.5]] and is an anti-[[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|Angel]]/[[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Alien]] variant of [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Coppermine]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 243
|rarity = UR
|name1 = Holy Coppermine
|name2 = Holy Coppermine, type κ
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Holy Coppermine, type κ''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Holy Coppermine is similar to [[Coppermine (Uber Rare Cat)|Coppermine]], being somewhere in-between her Evolved and [[True Form]] stat-wise with [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Alien]] targeting instead. She pairs well with [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet The Maiko]] in taking on tanky targets or swarms of melee enemies, and can even help them more reliably deal with ones that outrange them. Due to her foreswing length however, she can be rather unwieldy to use against enemies that have fast attack rates and a similar range to hers, such as [[Ursamajor]] and [[Angelic Sleipnir]]. [[Winged Pigge]] is probably her best matchup, as Holy Coppermine can completely shut down the pig's obnoxious, [[Weaken|Weaken]]-inducing attacks while standing at a somewhat comfortable distance from her.

Holy Coppermine unfortunately doesn't perform as well as the original Coppermine for DPS purposes, so you're better off using other units for that role, like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] for example. As is the case with many other old units, Holy Coppermine's usability will decline as the game progresses because of how much more aggressive enemies become, even with heavy boosting via [[Catseye]]s.

